 "examples": [
  {
   "question": "A hidden unit sees a weighted sum z = 2 in one example and z = −2 in another. Evaluate sigmoid, tanh, ReLU and leaky ReLU (α = 0.1) at both, and give the derivative of each at z = 2. A 3-class output layer then produces scores z = (2, 1, 0); find the softmax probabilities and check that they sum to 1.",
   "steps": [
    "Sigmoid at z = 2: e⁻² = 0.1353, so σ(2) = 1/(1 + 0.1353) = 1/1.1353 = 0.881.",
    "Sigmoid at z = −2: e² = 7.389, so σ(−2) = 1/(1 + 7.389) = 1/8.389 = 0.119.",
    "tanh at z = 2: (e² − e⁻²)/(e² + e⁻²) = (7.389 − 0.1353)/(7.389 + 0.1353) = 7.2537/7.5243 = 0.964.",
    "tanh at z = −2: by symmetry, −0.964.",
    "ReLU at z = 2 gives max(0, 2) = 2; at z = −2 gives max(0, −2) = 0.",
    "Leaky ReLU at z = 2 gives 2; at z = −2 gives 0.1 × (−2) = −0.2.",
    "Derivatives at z = 2: σ′(2) = 0.881 × (1 − 0.881) = 0.105; tanh′(2) = 1 − 0.964² = 0.070; ReLU′(2) = 1; leaky ReLU′(2) = 1.",
    "Softmax: e² = 7.389, e¹ = 2.718, e⁰ = 1.000; the sum is 11.107.",
    "Divide each by the sum: p = (7.389/11.107, 2.718/11.107, 1.000/11.107) = (0.665, 0.245, 0.090). Check: 0.665 + 0.245 + 0.090 = 1.000."
